      "number": 37625,
      "title": "[Flight] Preserve leading `U+FEFF` in text rows",
      "url": "https://github.com/react/react/pull/37625",
      "author": "unstubbable",
      "mergedAt": "2026-09-22T15:07:14Z",
      "labels": [
        "CLA Signed",
        "React Core Team"
      ],
      "hint": "unknown",
      "release": "⏳ 未リリース",
      "body": "The Flight client dropped a leading `U+FEFF` from outlined text rows when it decoded binary input. `TextDecoder` consumed the character as an encoding signature, even though it was part of the serialized string. Both the Node and Web decoders now use `ignoreBOM: true` to preserve it.\n\nRegression tests cover one and two leading U+FEFF characters with normal chunks and with every UTF-8 byte delivered separately. They also include an inline-string control. The global `TextDecoder` Flow declaration now makes `fatal` optional and declares `ignoreBOM`, matching the API.",
